                "source": "Twitter for iPad",
                "text": "In 2976 thousands more injured and adverse health effects for First Responders. John Mica chaired the Aviation subcommittee and I was the ranking Democrat. WE created the TSA - the idea being highly trained professional paid a good wage with benefits. The compromise because of pressure by the R\u2019s to keep private was that the TSA would not be on the GSA pay scale and could not unionize so turnover remained very high. Just a few years ago Congress fixed that and TSA workers were put on the GSA pay scale and allowed to unionize. Turnover dropped dramatically and threat detection went up significantly.  Trump stripped TSA of their union rights through an executive order and now another clueless incompetent appointed  Acting Administrator wants to go back to the good old private screening days.",
